  "name": "Wan 2.2 Image to Video + Lora",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Wan 2.2 Image to Video + Lora is a image to video workflow designed to animate a still image into a generated video clip using Wan 2.2. Its 19-node graph exposes 1 prompt/text field(s), 1 media input target(s), and 1 save/preview stage(s), while preserving the original editor-format graph for reference. The ComfyUI editor graph was converted to API format and is ready for live validation against the connected node and model registry.",
  "category": "Video & Animation",
  "subcategory": "Image to video",
  "episode": "EP06",
  "instructions": "1. Open the workflow and select Validate. SineForge will compare every node class and input against the currently connected ComfyUI instance without queueing it.\n2. Review the model-file entries in Requirements and place each checkpoint, text encoder, VAE, LoRA, or auxiliary model in the folder documented by the source workflow. Refresh ComfyUI after adding files.\n3. Upload and assign the required image, mask, video, or audio files to the listed media inputs. Keep the source dimensions and duration appropriate for the selected model.\n4. Set frame count, FPS, dimensions, conditioning strength, and seed. Start with one short clip to verify motion, identity, and memory use before scaling up.\n5. Save a copy before making structural changes. Use Editable inputs for normal parameters and Raw API JSON only when you need to inspect or change graph wiring.\n6. Validate again after every change. Queue one workflow only after validation passes; then inspect the returned output, logs, duration, dimensions, and media integrity.",
  "tags": [
    "EP06",
    "Image to video",
    "Video & Animation",
    "Wan 2.2"
  ],
